  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/e3732fa54055693d2a79b096871b7c04ac6f2add5b9b14b54f46ad4069aff6cf.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?",
  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{3}{5}$ on the left and $\\frac{3}{10}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/0c86de3f0d5e654938c06846cd77cd87e19b82d87e166fcfd0cabb1492ff4738.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $2$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $2$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right. \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}÷2=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $2.$",
